  "$comment": "Neobank research. Same discipline as the airdrop set: every figure carries a source and an as-of date, and a figure this pass could not attribute is null rather than estimated. Customer counts, transaction volume and revenue are three different measurements and are never substituted for one another.",
  "researchCutoff": "2026-08-23",
  "methodology": {
    "rankingMetric": "customers.value",
    "rankingRule": "Ranked by reported customer accounts. A neobank whose customer count this pass could not attribute to a source is listed with a null count and sorts last rather than being given an invented figure.",
    "customerCaveat": "Reported customer counts are registered accounts unless the entry says active. Registered and active are not comparable: Wise reports 15.6M active customers while several peers report every account ever opened. The basis is stated per row.",
    "volumeCaveat": "Transaction volume is only shown where a company reports one. Most consumer neobanks report deposits or revenue rather than throughput, so volume is null for them — it is never back-filled from revenue.",
    "revenueCaveat": "Revenue is the company's own reported top line for the stated period. Where a company reports in a currency other than USD the original figure is kept and the currency named."
  },
